The problem starts with Adam having 48 books. He sells 19 of them, leaving him with $48 - 19 = 29$ books. Adam then uses the money to buy 38 new books, which adds to his collection. Thus, the total number of books he has is $29 + 38 = 67$. Therefore, Adam would have $\boxed{67}$ books. 

